---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About · Unbeholden"
	description="Who runs Unbeholden, what it runs on, and why the data stays here."
>
	<p class="font-display text-statement mt-masthead mb-10 font-light text-pretty">
		I'm Jakub. I keep my own data, and run open source wherever there's a good version.
	</p>
	<div class="text-article">
		<p>
			I've never found a good reason to hand a company my photos and my mail when I don't have to.
			Convenience is the only argument for it, and running it myself has cost less than I expected.
		</p>
		<p class="text-dim mt-6">
			This site runs on hardware I own and a rented VPS. There are analytics, because I'd like to
			know which posts people actually read, but it's <a
				href="https://umami.is"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				class="text-accent">Umami</a
			> on my own box: no cookies, and nothing
			about you leaves it.
		</p>
		<p class="text-dim mt-6">
			When something I need doesn't exist, or only exists as a service someone could take away, I
			write it myself and publish it here. It's usually small and solves one specific problem.
		</p>
		<p class="text-dim mt-6">
			If any of it's useful to you, good. Copy what you like, and maybe you'll find something you
			didn't know you could run yourself.
		</p>
		<p class="text-dim mt-6 mb-12">Prose is CC BY 4.0. Code is CC0/MIT.</p>
	</div>
	<div
		class="border-rule text-nav grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr))] gap-x-8 border-t leading-[1.7]"
	>
		<a href="mailto:hello@unbeholden.dev" class="border-rule border-b py-4"
			>Email<br /><span class="text-faint italic">hello@unbeholden.dev</span></a
		>
		<a href="/feed.xml" class="border-rule text-accent border-b py-4"
			>Feed<br /><span class="text-faint italic">unbeholden.dev/feed.xml</span></a
		>
	</div>
</Layout>
